WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.200
Grunt work that it can manage too, right?

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.220
we've spent months trying to get it to work with the CAD models and it's

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.540
just not doing very well.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.120
And I think that's okay because I think plenty of us actually enjoy doing

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.940
CAD, you know?

00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:23.087
It's very good at image analysis spatial analysis things like that it's

00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:24.567
not there yet.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:28.807
it doesn't live in the 3D world with us it's all just code and stuff

00:00:29.186 --> 00:00:32.246
As far as like the culture, though, like I think there has to be a balance.

00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:33.406
Like we have to use it.

00:00:33.226 --> 00:00:35.466
We can't say, hey, we're not going to touch that.

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:39.946
That being said, I'm probably overusing it — probably underusing it.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.680
You've got to find the balance where you use it, but you understand how

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.967
you're using it and what it's doing.
